# Lock Protocol

Spec: Locks
Purpose:
  Define the resource locking protocol that prevents concurrent
  modification of shared resources by multiple agents. Locks are
  acquired before tool execution and released after task completion.

Owns: governance/locks.sdd

## Lock Types

  READ       — Multiple readers allowed, no writers
  WRITE      — Exclusive write access, blocks all others
  EXCLUSIVE  — Full exclusive access (read + write + delete)
  MIGRATION  — Database migration lock (blocks all schema changes)
  DEPLOYMENT — Deployment lock (blocks all writes to target environment)

## Lock Acquisition Protocol

  1. AI resolves capability → resource
  2. AI requests lock on resource
  3. LockManager checks current holders
  4. If conflict → BLOCK with reason
  5. If clear → grant lock
  6. AI performs action
  7. AI releases lock (or auto-release on task complete)

## Lock Compatibility Matrix

                  READ    WRITE    EXCLUSIVE    MIGRATION    DEPLOYMENT
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  READ            ✓       ✗        ✗             ✗             ✗
  WRITE           ✗       ✗        ✗             ✗             ✗
  EXCLUSIVE       ✗       ✗        ✗             ✗             ✗
  MIGRATION       ✗       ✗        ✗             ✗             ✗
  DEPLOYMENT      ✗       ✗        ✗             ✗             ✗

## Lock Scope

  TASK     — Locked for duration of task (auto-release on task complete)
  SESSION  — Locked for duration of agent session
  MANUAL   — Must be explicitly released

## Lock Manager

  @agent.lock-manager
    ECC equivalent: agent.supervisor

  Responsibilities:
    - Grant/revoke locks
    - Detect deadlocks
    - Enforce lock timeouts
    - Audit lock events

## Lock Events

  @lock_event.LE1

  action: acquire
  resource: @resource.source-code
  agent: @agent.backend
  task: @task.T2041
  type: WRITE
  result: GRANTED
  timestamp: 2026-09-01T16:30:00Z

  @lock_event.LE2

  action: acquire
  resource: @resource.source-code
  agent: @agent.backend
  task: @task.T2042
  type: WRITE
  result: DENIED
  reason: T2041 holds WRITE lock
  timestamp: 2026-09-01T16:31:00Z

## Deadlock Prevention

  - Lock timeout: 30 minutes
  - Circular wait detection via graph analysis
  - Lock escalation: multiple READ → single WRITE (if owner)

## Scheduler Integration

  Scheduler checks locks before task assignment:

    READY TASKS
      → resolve required resources
      → check locks on those resources
      → only assign to agent if locks can be acquired

